quickstart plan — backend=docker
  workspace  /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws
  suite      /root/e2e/accept/demo/docker-suites/tbench-pilot-docker
  agents-dir /root/e2e/accept/aeval/agents
  repo root  /root/e2e/accept/aeval
  note: the suite lets the sandbox dial registry.npmjs.org, nodejs.org, 193.126.4.2; the broker binds 193.126.4.2 so that route exists
  note: /root/e2e/accept/aeval/agents already declares deepagent, dsh, fakeagent
  note: tbench-pilot-docker is already pinned to docker — used as it is
steps:
   1. docker-preflight probe the local docker daemon
      runs: docker info --format {{.ServerVersion}}
   2. tls             generate the CA and the gateway certificate
      writes /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/tls/{ca.crt,ca.key,gateway.crt,gateway.key} (the SAN covers the sandbox-facing host address)
   3. token-counter   serve the trusted token counter on 127.0.0.1:8792
      starts an in-process HTTP server; writes nothing
   4. broker-spec     write the broker spec
      writes /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/broker.json (0600: upstream identity, limits, TLS material, token-counter endpoint)
   5. run             run the suite end to end (harbor harbor + the aeval plugin)
      writes /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/run/ and /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/run.sqlite3
   6. evidence-links  link the trial evidence into runs/trials/
      writes /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/runs/trials/<trial> symlinks
   7. report          render report.md from the store
      runs: aeval report <run-id> --store /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/run.sqlite3 --k 1 > /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/report.md
   8. dashboard       render dashboard.html from the store
      writes /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/dashboard.html
   9. recompute       recompute the sealed bundle (independent re-derivation)
      runs: aeval recompute /root/e2e/accept/demo/ws/run
  10. verdict         score the run with aeval's own reliability metric
      reads the sealed run and its store; writes nothing
